<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>

    <!-- Indonesian rupiah has no circulating subunit: every price is whole
         rupiah. Odoo ships IDR with rounding 0.01 (base/data/res_currency_data.xml),
         so every amount renders with two decimals — "Rp 200,000.00".

         `res.currency.decimal_places` is a stored *computed* field derived from
         rounding, and it is readonly:

             @api.depends('rounding')
             def _compute_decimal_places(self):
                 if 0 < currency.rounding < 1:
                     currency.decimal_places = ceil(log10(1 / currency.rounding))
                 else:
                     currency.decimal_places = 0

         So rounding is the only writable knob, and 1 is the value that yields
         decimal_places = 0 -> "Rp 200,000".

         WHY A <function> AND NOT <record id="base.IDR">:
         base wraps its currency data in <data noupdate="1">, so the ir_model_data
         row for base.IDR has noupdate = true. A <record> pointing at it is
         therefore SKIPPED on module upgrade (it would only take effect on a fresh
         install). <function> is always executed, so this applies on install and
         on every update, and is idempotent.

         This is a localisation change rather than a layout one, and it is
         deliberately global: money should read the same in the POS, on invoices
         and in reports. Rounding to whole rupiah also means totals no longer
         carry fractions nobody can pay. Remove this file if sen is ever needed
         back. -->
    <function name="write" model="res.currency">
        <function name="search" model="res.currency">
            <value eval="[('name', '=', 'IDR')]"/>
        </function>
        <value eval="{'rounding': 1}"/>
    </function>

</odoo>
